config PON_RTL9602C
	tristate "Realtek RTL9602C GPON MAC"
	depends on NET_DSA_RTL9602C
	depends on RTL9602C_ETH || !RTL9602C_ETH
	select AUXILIARY_BUS
	select PON
	help
	  Driver of the GPON MAC, the PON MAC behind it, the GEM ports and the
	  OMCI channel of the Realtek RTL9602C, the chip of GPON ONUs such as
	  SFP sticks. It registers the ONU with the PON class: its activation
	  state machine, its OMCI port and a network interface per GEM port.

	  The MAC sits behind the PON port of the chip's switch, in the same
	  register window and behind the same interrupt, so the switch driver,
	  NET_DSA_RTL9602C, makes the auxiliary device this driver binds to and
	  offers it its services. Without this driver the switch works, but the
	  PON port cannot be enabled.

	  Say Y or M on an RTL9602C board. To compile this driver as a module,
	  choose M here: the module will be called rtl9602c-pon.

config PON_RTL9602C_PLOAM_INJECT
	bool "Inject downstream PLOAM messages through debugfs"
	depends on PON_RTL9602C && DEBUG_FS
	help
	  Give the switch's debugfs directory a file, rtl9602c/ploaminject. A
	  write of the twelve octets of a downstream PLOAM message, in hex,
	  hands the message to the activation state machine as if the OLT had
	  sent it, so that what the OLT at hand never sends, such as
	  Disable_Serial_Number and POPUP, can be tested. A process that can
	  write the file can stop the ONU or take it off the PON, so the
	  option is for test images, not for an ONU in service.

	  If unsure, say N.
